  "id": "social-intervention",
  "term": "social intervention",
  "definition": "A social intervention is a program, in this context within primary health care, that aims to address individual and community social needs. Its successful implementation is described as relying on creativity, persistence, partnership, understanding those needs, and overcoming barriers.",
